{"id":"insert-delete-getrandom-o1","title":"Insert Delete GetRandom O(1)","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Design","tags":["Array","Hash Table","Math","Design","Randomized"],"companies":{"google":3,"apple":3,"meta":4,"amazon":3,"microsoft":3},"kind":"design","class_name":"RandomizedSet","description":"Implement a set of integers that supports three operations in **average O(1)** time:\n\n- `RandomizedSet()` creates an empty set.\n- `insert(val)` adds `val` and returns `true`; returns `false` if it was already present.\n- `remove(val)` deletes `val` and returns `true`; returns `false` if it was not present.\n- `getRandom()` returns one of the current elements, each with equal probability. It is only called when the set is non-empty.\n\nBecause `getRandom` is random, the judge only calls it when the set contains **exactly one element**, so its output is determined. Your implementation must still be uniformly random in general.","examples":[{"input":"[\"RandomizedSet\",\"insert\",\"remove\",\"insert\",\"remove\",\"getRandom\",\"insert\",\"remove\",\"insert\",\"getRandom\"]\n[[],[1],[2],[2],[1],[],[2],[2],[5],[]]","output":"[null,true,false,true,true,2,false,true,true,5]","explanation":"remove(2) fails before 2 is inserted. After removing 1 the only element is 2, so getRandom returns 2. Inserting 2 again fails because it is already present."}],"constraints":["-2^31 <= val <= 2^31 - 1","At most 2 * 10^5 calls in total","getRandom is only called on a non-empty set"],"hints":["A hash set gives O(1) insert and remove, but picking a uniformly random element from it is not O(1). An array gives O(1) random access but O(n) removal.","Use both: a list of values and a dict from value to its index in the list.","To remove in O(1), swap the element with the last element of the list, fix the dict entry of the moved element, then pop."],"starter":"class RandomizedSet:\n    def __init__(self):\n        pass\n\n    def insert(self, val: int) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n    def remove(self, val: int) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n    def getRandom(self) -> int:\n        pass\n","compare":"exact","tests":[{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["insert",[1]],["remove",[2]],["insert",[2]],["remove",[1]],["getRandom",[]],["insert",[2]],["remove",[2]],["insert",[5]],["getRandom",[]]]},"output":[null,true,false,true,true,2,false,true,true,5]},{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["remove",[0]],["insert",[0]],["insert",[0]],["getRandom",[]],["remove",[0]],["remove",[0]]]},"output":[null,false,true,false,0,true,false]},{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["insert",[10]],["insert",[20]],["insert",[30]],["remove",[20]],["remove",[10]],["getRandom",[]],["remove",[30]],["remove",[30]],["insert",[20]],["getRandom",[]]]},"output":[null,true,true,true,true,true,30,true,false,true,20]},{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["insert",[-5]],["insert",[2147483647]],["remove",[-5]],["getRandom",[]],["insert",[-5]],["remove",[2147483647]],["getRandom",[]]]},"output":[null,true,true,true,2147483647,true,true,-5]},{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["insert",[1]],["insert",[2]],["insert",[3]],["remove",[1]],["remove",[3]],["getRandom",[]],["insert",[1]],["remove",[2]],["getRandom",[]]]},"output":[null,true,true,true,true,true,2,true,true,1]},{"input":{"ops":[["RandomizedSet",[]],["insert",[0]],["insert",[1]],["insert",[2]],["insert",[3]],["insert",[4]],["insert",[5]],["insert",[6]],["insert",[7]],["insert",[8]],["insert",[9]],["insert",[10]],["insert",[11]],["insert",[12]],["insert",[13]],["insert",[14]],["insert",[15]],["insert",[16]],["insert",[17]],["insert",[18]],["insert",[19]],["insert",[20]],["insert",[21]],["insert",[22]],["insert",[23]],["insert",[24]],["insert",[25]],["insert",[26]],["insert",[27]],["insert",[28]],["insert",[29]],["insert",[30]],["insert",[31]],["insert",[32]],["insert",[33]],["insert",[34]],["insert",[35]],["insert",[36]],["insert",[37]],["insert",[38]],["insert",[39]],["insert",[40]],["insert",[41]],["insert",[42]],["insert",[43]],["insert",